          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe4037cdb4a15965470da7d5afc96a1df404c98d238f21ab6be3a0198428b843:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f1368a3892fd4bd0bb5c5526c1cb70cd",
      "statement": "FindMissingSections is a line scanner, not a markdown parser: it splits the body on '\\n', trims each line, opens a section only on a line starting with the literal '## ', records the trimmed remainder as the section name, and marks that section filled on the first line that is not empty content — with case-insensitive set membership so heading casing is irrelevant and any single non-empty line counts as content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/Issues/SpecTemplateValidator.cs#L17-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1883b0558010252ee8588c775560236511c28e56bcf5901cf898755e140a4c8d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f5037f0535d4467a9a7b6c0ad29f4e7",
      "statement": "Empty content is defined as an empty (or whitespace-only, post-trim) line, a line starting with `<!--`, or a line equal to `_No response_` case-insensitively; content before the first `## ` heading is discarded because no section is open yet, and a null body therefore reports all seven sections missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/Issues/SpecTemplateValidator.cs#L32-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:280b02627ddb7589ebfb5388a39449ca6201a14a46c93248c95ecc0a23a61630:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/GitHub/Issues/SpecTemplateValidatorTests.cs#L114-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30ae2abbcc4ae64c742fd8c8d84f27df9678742556c86851ae1aa42cc7a83e2c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/GitHub/Issues/SpecTemplateValidatorTests.cs#L34-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:55a34cd2b02fd90cfa49fe5192186cdba8a5ca5e4502db2720ed686fcbb8dbfc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53c9a470d81a46eeb223f35f3970882a",
      "statement": "The parser's line-scanning approach means only the opening line of a multi-line HTML comment is ignored (continuation lines count as content), fenced code blocks are not tracked so a `## ` line inside a fence is read as a real heading, and headings with one hash or three hashes do not open a section — whitespace only body content before the first heading is dropped.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/Issues/SpecTemplateValidator.cs#L22-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:508ec0821d6e8fb5312b54856ab040331a4272c470c457789e38c1dc3c552c4d:"
        },
