          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db68c0d10eafc36191a269a4941bdf8153d6756ab72d40471079ae8d31d769a0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c2309d68d7fa42c2beb09aa4b65801cf",
      "statement": "An invalid spec is handled by a fixed, ordered, uncaught pair of GitHub writes — PostCommentAsync with the body `Closed: the spec is missing required sections: <names>.` and then CloseIssueAsync which sets state closed with state_reason not_planned — followed by a Debug log and a return that prevents enqueueing; a failure in either call propagates out of the webhook handler instead of being swallowed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L40-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0d35813228612814134624f4040cb51d61aac022ec123b62b02fe07731be9c3d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L131-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64560b01a75711a84e70d05d67b98f135910ac93d133c377fe3bd68a23e90579:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L63-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:062bc5641f5d7259ea2fe436c2371a85b55a9b03c5fa824ef718db8beffd4353:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aea4e7fef4774d91af54e2b8fcb1c8d8",
      "statement": "Section validation outranks maintainer approval: the missing-section check and its return execute before the `ready-for-agent` check in the same handler, so an already-approved issue is still closed as not_planned when a required section is empty, and a closed issue can only re-enter the gate through a reopened or re-label delivery.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L61-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a57948c10663a578d18d72e516e22dbad6c120563b09eff77bf6134d4475ed9b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_159e231ac68145669c7ba7f9b95ea03f",
      "statement": "A complete spec that also carries `ready-for-agent` is turned into an ImplementSpec job built from the webhook payload's title and body and offered to JobQueue.TryAdd, with admission logged at Information and a duplicate-key rejection logged only at Debug — the processor neither throws nor comments when admission is refused.",
      "evidence": [
